devel/stirmake: Add stirmake version 0.4.4

Packaged in wip by Juha-Matti Tilli

This package provides stirmake version 0.4.4

Stirmake is a fast build tool intended to make recursive build systems
with possible git submodules easy to create. It is programmable in the
custom programming language Amyplan. The intention is that with
stirmake, one never has to do the equivalent of "make clean" to fix a
broken build.

Stirmake can be built without dependencies, with Lua, or with LuaJIT.
Using Lua has no benefit over the embedded language Amyplan (unless one
is familiar with Lua already, or unless one uses a Stirfile developed on
a machine with LuaJIT that needs to be later used on a platform without
LuaJIT support), but using LuaJIT has a speed benefit.

Peculiarities of the provided package:

1. Stirmake can be built with a prior installed version of stirmake,
with GNU make or with a bootstrap shell script. It cannot be built with
BSD make. Since GNU make would be a heavyweight build dependency, here
the bootstrap script is used. Unfortunately, the bootstrap script is
single-threaded. Fortunately, stirmake still builds in an acceptable
time.

2. The CC, CFLAGS and LDFLAGS variables need to be passed in the
environment.

3. If STIR_WITH_LUA is set to 1, both STIR_LUAINCS and STIR_LUALIBS need
to be set, or else the build system of stirmake uses pkg-config to
deduce their values. However, pkgsrc buildlink already sets the include
paths in CFLAGS. So, place a dummy "-I." to STIR_LUAINCS to suppress the
pkg-config.
